// =============================================================================
// Toggle-closure waiver elfile — structurally-unreachable toggle bits
// =============================================================================
// Tracker : doc/toggle_closure_plan.md §二-A(b) + §七.4 item 6
// Source  : doc/toggle_closure_coverage_report_20260726.md §三 (per-signal
//           verification). Every entry below was traced to an RTL constant
//           assignment or a constant module-port binding, i.e. the signal
//           physically cannot change value in ANY simulation.
// Policy  : ONLY constant-driven signals. No functional/behavioural toggle is
//           waived. Stimulus-reachable gaps stay uncovered and are tracked as
//           closure work (plan §七.4 items 1-5 = T-B2/T-D2/T-F2/T-G2/T-H2).
// Usage   : urg ... -elfile simu/exclude_v4.tgl -elfile simu/fullexclude.tgl
//           ADDITIVE to exclude_v4.tgl (reset nets + DFT/ICG enables).
// Review  : requires second reviewer sign-off before final coverage signoff.
//
// ── URG elfile syntax notes (established empirically, 2026-07-26) ────────────
//  * The decl string must match the URG report label, with the range AFTER the
//    name:  Toggle sig "logic sig[27:0]"    <- WORKS
//    NOT the RTL declaration order:
//           Toggle sig "logic [27:0] sig"   <- silently ignored (no delta)
//  * Per-bit slices (`Toggle sig[0] "logic sig[0]"`) are NOT honoured for
//    vectors by this URG version — verified by A/B run: 2-bit slice gave 0.00
//    delta while the whole-signal form gave the expected +0.03 TOGGLE.
//    Consequence: a vector can only be waived in whole. Signals whose vector
//    contains BOTH constant and functional bits are therefore NOT waived here
//    (see the iutlb_off_flg / dutlb_off_flg note at the bottom).
//  * CHECKSUM lines are required; without them URG emits UCAPI-EL-MCM
//    "module checksum mismatch" and drops the exclusion. Values are copied
//    from exclude_v4.tgl (same design build).
// =============================================================================

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// (1) mmu_l1dtlb_hit_rd.dutlb_off_pgs / dutlb_pre_pgs — tied to 3'b0
//     RTL (mmu_l1dtlb_hit_rd.sv:257):  assign dutlb_off_pgs = 3'b0; // 4K default
//     RTL (mmu_l1dtlb_hit_rd.sv:273):  assign dutlb_pre_pgs = dutlb_off_pgs;
//     The off/direct-map path is 4K-only by construction, so all 3 bits of both
//     nets are constant 0 → 0->1 unreachable. Both hit_rd ports affected.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// CHECKSUM: "32988409 4228649183"
// ANNOTATION: "ModuleName: mmu_l1dtlb_hit_rd"
INSTANCE: tb_top.u_dut.u_mmu_l1dtlb.x_hit_rd_port0
//
Toggle dutlb_off_pgs "logic dutlb_off_pgs[2:0]"
Toggle dutlb_pre_pgs "logic dutlb_pre_pgs[2:0]"

// CHECKSUM: "32988409 4228649183"
// ANNOTATION: "ModuleName: mmu_l1dtlb_hit_rd"
INSTANCE: tb_top.u_dut.u_mmu_l1dtlb.x_hit_rd_port1
//
Toggle dutlb_off_pgs "logic dutlb_off_pgs[2:0]"
Toggle dutlb_pre_pgs "logic dutlb_pre_pgs[2:0]"

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// (2) mmu_l1dtlb.lsu_mmu_stamo_pa0[27:0] — tied to zero
//     RTL (mmu_l1dtlb.sv:563):
//       assign lsu_mmu_stamo_pa0[PPN_WIDTH-1:0] = {PPN_WIDTH{1'b0}};
//     STAMO (store-atomic) PA input is unconnected in this integration; all
//     28 bits are constant 0 → 0->1 unreachable by construction.
//     Measured effect of this single waiver: TOGGLE 77.73 -> 77.76.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// CHECKSUM: "715530975 445175681"
// ANNOTATION: "ModuleName: mmu_l1dtlb"
INSTANCE: tb_top.u_dut.u_mmu_l1dtlb
//
Toggle lsu_mmu_stamo_pa0 "logic lsu_mmu_stamo_pa0[27:0]"

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// (3) mmu_l1dtlb_allocator.req0_port_id / req1_port_id — constant bindings
//     RTL (mmu_l1dtlb.sv:826/832):  .req0_port_id(1'b0), .req1_port_id(1'b1)
//     PORT_WIDTH=1 and each port is bound to a literal, so inside the
//     allocator req0_port_id is always 0 and req1_port_id is always 1.
//     (This is why plan task T-E was cancelled — confirmed in report §三.)
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// CHECKSUM: "2801342751 2375986322"
// ANNOTATION: "ModuleName: mmu_l1dtlb_allocator"
INSTANCE: tb_top.u_dut.u_mmu_l1dtlb.x_allocator
//
Toggle req0_port_id "logic req0_port_id"
Toggle req1_port_id "logic req1_port_id"

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// (4) mmu_l1dtlb_expt_cam.expt_wr1_acflt — tied to zero
//     RTL (mmu_l1dtlb.sv:323):  assign expt_wr1_acflt = 1'b0;
//     The JTLB write port cannot report an access fault in this design (only
//     the PTW port wr0 can), so the CAM's wr1 acflt input is a dead net.
//     Previously paper-tracked in the exclude_v4.tgl header; expressed here so
//     it is actually removed from the toggle denominator.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// CHECKSUM: "2951616054 3457367824"
// ANNOTATION: "ModuleName: mmu_l1dtlb_expt_cam"
INSTANCE: tb_top.u_dut.u_mmu_l1dtlb.x_l1dtlb_expt_cam
//
Toggle expt_wr1_acflt "logic expt_wr1_acflt"

// =============================================================================
// DELIBERATELY *NOT* WAIVED — mixed constant/functional vectors
// =============================================================================
// iutlb_off_flg (mmu_l1itlb.sv:2232) and dutlb_off_flg / dutlb_pre_flg
// (mmu_l1dtlb_hit_rd.sv:256,272) have the form
//     {sysmap_flg[4:0], 5'b00110, 3'b111, 1'b1}
// URG scores them in two chunks:
//     [13:10] -> already COVERED (driven by sysmap_mmu_flg*[4:1])
//     [ 9: 0] -> reported uncovered
// Bits [8:0] are the literal constants and are genuinely unreachable, BUT
// bit [9] is driven by sysmap_mmu_flg*[0], which IS functionally reachable.
// Because this URG version ignores per-bit Toggle slices (see syntax notes),
// waiving the [9:0] chunk would also waive the reachable bit [9] — that would
// be over-waiving, so these nets are left uncovered on purpose.
// Correct closure path for bit [9]: drive sysmap flg bit0 = 1 while taking the
// off/M-mode path (sysmap_window(..., 5'b00001) + M-mode access). T-C already
// does the port0/port1 in-SO rounds; extending them to the off path is tracked
// as a follow-up rather than hidden behind a waiver.
// =============================================================================
